1111:   \label{thm:fga_pic_representability_etale}
1112:   \lean{AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fgaPicardRepresentability}
1113:   \uses{def:pic_et_sheaf, lem:pic_et_is_sheaf, def:rel_pic_sharp}
1114:   Let \(k\) be a field and \(C/k\) a smooth proper geometrically integral
1115:   curve --- with \emph{no} hypothesis on \(C(k)\). Then:
1116:   \begin{enumerate}
1117:     \item the \'etale-sheafified relative Picard functor \(\Pic_{(C/k)\et}\) of
1118:       \cref{def:pic_et_sheaf} is representable by a \(k\)-scheme that is
1119:       separated and locally of finite type over \(k\); and
1120:     \item if \(C\) has a \(k\)-rational point, the comparison
1121:       \(\Pic^\sharp_{C/k} \to \Pic_{(C/k)\et}\) is an isomorphism.
1122:   \end{enumerate}
1123: 
1124:   This is the project's central open obligation, and it is expected to remain
1125:   open. It is the only assertion of this chapter that is not proved, and the
1126:   Jacobian headline (\cref{chap:Jacobian}) rests on it.
